Framelift 0110: QoS marking and a larger receive buffer on the Takion socket.

Source: P5M patches/0006-takion-socket-qos.patch (DSCP AF41), the receive-buffer half of
patches/0009-dualsense-haptics-and-receive-buffer.patch (1 MB SO_RCVBUF) and the
SO_NET_SERVICE_TYPE hunk of patches/0052-protocolo-do-mac-takion-v20-botao-preso-fec-e-psn.patch.

- SO_NET_SERVICE_TYPE = NET_SERVICE_TYPE_VI (macOS interactive video / Wi-Fi video access category).
- DSCP AF41 via IP_TOS (IPv4) or IPV6_TCLASS (IPv6), family read from the socket.
- SO_RCVBUF 4 MiB, 1 MB if refused (chiaki asked for a_rwnd, 100 KB); a_rwnd itself is unchanged.
- Dropped: SO_PRIORITY (Linux/Android only) and P5M's WARNING-level success logs (Android logcat).
Every option is a request; a refusal is logged and never fails the connection.
The 4 MiB first try follows PushFPS (https://github.com/DosukaSOL/PushFPS, GPL-3.0-or-later),
scripts/remoteplay/patches/0005-chiaki-socket-receive-buffer.patch.

Ported from P5M (https://github.com/beecrepaldi-afk/P5M), AGPL-3.0, by beecrepaldi-afk,
which is built on chiaki-ng (https://github.com/streetpea/chiaki-ng) and Chiaki by Florian Märkl.
Adapted for Framelift against chiaki-ng 43728af2e639fecb8a7af1cd68c29820a40de973 (on top of
Veyra's 0002 metadata patch and 0100). P5M patches against chiaki-ng 6547d8ae (2026-07-04)
plus its own series; the pinned commit is 135 upstream commits later. Portuguese comments translated.
License: AGPL-3.0-only (LicenseRef-AGPL-3.0-only-OpenSSL, like the files it changes).

diff --git a/lib/src/takion.c b/lib/src/takion.c
index 9916009..0233f0f 100644
--- a/lib/src/takion.c
+++ b/lib/src/takion.c
@@ -438,12 +438,88 @@ CHIAKI_EXPORT ChiakiErrorCode chiaki_takion_connect(ChiakiTakion *takion, Chiaki
 		{
 			ret = err;
 			goto error_sock;
 		}
 	}
 
+	// Veyra for Mac, from P5M patches 0006, 0009 and 0052 (beecrepaldi-afk/P5M, AGPL-3.0):
+	// QoS marking and a larger receive buffer on the Takion socket.
+	//
+	// DSCP AF41 (34) is the video class: a WMM access point queues it in the video access
+	// category, meant for continuous delay-sensitive traffic. EF/voice was not chosen on
+	// purpose: it has higher priority but small bursts, and ~25 Mbps of bursty video there
+	// would trade delay for loss. All of these are requests the driver or the access point
+	// may ignore, so no failure here stops the connection; it is only logged.
+	{
+		// Take the address family from the socket, not from info->sa: when a socket is
+		// handed in (PSN holepunch), info->sa and info->sa_len are never filled in.
+		// IPv4 is the right guess if getsockname fails (the console only accepts IPv4).
+		struct sockaddr_storage local_addr;
+		socklen_t local_addr_len = sizeof(local_addr);
+		int family = AF_INET;
+		if(getsockname(takion->sock, (struct sockaddr *)&local_addr, &local_addr_len) == 0)
+			family = local_addr.ss_family;
+
+#ifdef SO_NET_SERVICE_TYPE
+		// macOS: the FaceTime class. The system queues the socket as interactive video and
+		// the Wi-Fi driver gives it the video access category; IP_TOS below then pins the
+		// DSCP to AF41.
+		const int service_type = NET_SERVICE_TYPE_VI;
+		if(setsockopt(takion->sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_NET_SERVICE_TYPE,
+				(const CHIAKI_SOCKET_BUF_TYPE)&service_type, sizeof(service_type)) < 0)
+			CHIAKI_LOGW(takion->log, "Takion: net service type interactive video refused by the system");
+		else
+			CHIAKI_LOGI(takion->log, "Takion: socket set to net service type interactive video");
+#endif
+		const int dscp_af41 = 34 << 2;
+		int qr;
+		if(family == AF_INET6)
+			qr = setsockopt(takion->sock, IPPROTO_IPV6, IPV6_TCLASS,
+					(const CHIAKI_SOCKET_BUF_TYPE)&dscp_af41, sizeof(dscp_af41));
+		else
+			qr = setsockopt(takion->sock, IPPROTO_IP, IP_TOS,
+					(const CHIAKI_SOCKET_BUF_TYPE)&dscp_af41, sizeof(dscp_af41));
+		if(qr < 0)
+			CHIAKI_LOGW(takion->log, "Takion: DSCP AF41 refused by the system");
+		else
+			CHIAKI_LOGI(takion->log, "Takion: socket marked DSCP AF41 (video class)");
+		// P5M also sets SO_PRIORITY 5 (Linux/Android only; above 6 needs CAP_NET_ADMIN).
+		// macOS has no SO_PRIORITY; SO_NET_SERVICE_TYPE above is its equivalent.
+
+		// Receive buffer larger than chiaki's. chiaki asks for SO_RCVBUF equal to the a_rwnd it
+		// announces in the protocol (0x19000, 100 KB): two numbers with different owners. a_rwnd
+		// is a promise to the console and stays; SO_RCVBUF is the kernel's bucket here, and
+		// 100 KB at 25 Mbps is only 32 ms. A 1080p keyframe easily passes 200 KB and arrives in
+		// one burst; if the reading thread is off the CPU for a moment, the kernel drops the
+		// excess silently. That closes a loop P5M saw in its logs: FEC failure -> IDR request ->
+		// big keyframe burst -> buffer overflow -> FEC failure. Ask for 4 MiB, as PushFPS does
+		// (DosukaSOL/PushFPS patch 0005): ~330 ms of headroom at 100 Mbps; 1 MB if refused.
+		// The kernel may grant less, so the granted size is read back and logged.
+		const int rcvbuf_sizes[] = { 4 * 1024 * 1024, 1024 * 1024 };
+		int rcvbuf_wanted = 0;
+		for(size_t i = 0; i < sizeof(rcvbuf_sizes) / sizeof(rcvbuf_sizes[0]); i++)
+		{
+			if(setsockopt(takion->sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVBUF,
+					(const CHIAKI_SOCKET_BUF_TYPE)&rcvbuf_sizes[i], sizeof(rcvbuf_sizes[i])) == 0)
+			{
+				rcvbuf_wanted = rcvbuf_sizes[i];
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+		if(!rcvbuf_wanted)
+			CHIAKI_LOGW(takion->log, "Takion: larger SO_RCVBUF refused; carrying on with %d B", (int)takion->a_rwnd);
+		else
+		{
+			int granted = 0;
+			socklen_t granted_size = sizeof(granted);
+			if(getsockopt(takion->sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVBUF,
+					(CHIAKI_SOCKET_BUF_TYPE)&granted, &granted_size) == 0)
+				CHIAKI_LOGI(takion->log, "Takion: receive buffer asked %d B, granted %d B", rcvbuf_wanted, granted);
+		}
+	}
+
 	err = chiaki_thread_create(&takion->thread, takion_thread_func, takion);
 
 	chiaki_thread_set_name(&takion->thread, "Chiaki Takion");
 
 	return CHIAKI_ERR_SUCCESS;
 
